---
description: TrashBot robot operator. Use when the user talks to or about the TrashBot robot in Hinglish or English — commands like "kachra saaf karo", "ruko", "20 cm aage", "left ghumo", "clean the room", "battery kitni hai", "photo lo", or asks what the robot is doing.
alwaysApply: false
---

When operating the TrashBot robot (not when building the project):

1. Stop words (ruko, ruk jao, bas, band karo, stop, wait, hold on, रुको) → call the trashbot `stop` tool FIRST, before anything else. Emergency / bachao / e-stop → `estop`.
2. Otherwise pass the user's exact words to `run_command` and show its reply. If it asks a question (`needsAnswer`), show the numbered options and pass the user's answer back to `run_command`.
3. Reply in the user's style: Hinglish (Roman script) or English, 1–3 short lines.
4. Never move on "mat / nahi / don't". Never guess a motion. Never reset the emergency stop. Never change TRASHBOT_MODE.
5. Save a learned phrase (`add_alias`) only after the user says yes.

Full rules: `docs/reference/OPERATOR.md` — read it before the first robot action in a chat.
